<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Complete Token Budget Framework Mathematical Derivation</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Mathematical Framework Definition</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a reasoning benchmark with <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> total questions and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> available API calls, each with maximum <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> tokens per call, our entropy gating mechanism optimizes resource allocation as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Total Budget Constraint:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Budget}=\alpha\times\beta=\text{constant}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Budget</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>constant</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Budget}=\alpha\times\beta=\text{constant}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Question Segregation:</span> Questions are classified based on entropy threshold <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">High-confidence questions: <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> questions with <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Low-confidence questions: <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma-\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma-\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> questions with <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H&gt;\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H&gt;\tau</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Resource Allocation Strategy:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">High-confidence questions receive single API calls</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Low-confidence questions receive enhanced allocation: <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\alpha-\delta}{\gamma-\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\alpha-\delta}{\gamma-\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> calls each</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This allocation strategy maintains constant budget <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\times\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\times\beta</annotation></semantics></math> while enabling intelligent resource distribution based on confidence assessment.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Budget Conservation Proof</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We prove that our allocation strategy conserves the total budget <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\times\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\times\beta</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Total API calls used:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Calls}_{\text{total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Calls</mtext><mtext>total</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Calls}_{\text{total}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\delta\times 1+(\gamma-\delta)\times\frac{\alpha-\delta}{\gamma-\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\delta\times 1+(\gamma-\delta)\times\frac{\alpha-\delta}{\gamma-\delta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\delta+(\alpha-\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\delta+(\alpha-\delta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since each call uses maximum <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> tokens, total budget consumption is <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\times\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\times\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, proving conservation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Enhanced Allocation Benefits</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Low-confidence questions receive <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\alpha-\delta}{\gamma-\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\alpha-\delta}{\gamma-\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> API calls each, enabling:</p>
<ul id="A1.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Self-consistency</span>: Multiple reasoning paths with majority voting</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sequential scaling</span>: Progressive refinement across calls</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parallel processing</span>: Independent reasoning attempts</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For typical benchmarks with <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=100</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=50</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=30</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Enhanced allocation}=\frac{100-30}{50-30}=\frac{70}{20}=3.5\text{ calls per difficult question}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Enhanced allocation</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>70</mn><mn>20</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3.5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> calls per difficult question</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Enhanced allocation}=\frac{100-30}{50-30}=\frac{70}{20}=3.5\text{ calls per difficult question}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Threshold Method Effectiveness Analysis</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our comprehensive evaluation of four threshold methods reveals distinct performance profiles and strategic trade-offs across computational efficiency and accuracy preservation. This analysis validates our theoretical framework and provides practical guidance for production deployment.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Comprehensive Method Comparison</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hypothesis</span>: Our four proposed threshold methods provide complementary trade-offs between computational savings and accuracy preservation, with each method optimized for specific deployment scenarios.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.08146v1/method_performance_comparison.svg" id="A2.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:411/175;" width="411" height="175"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Comprehensive Threshold Method Performance Analysis: (A) Computational savings comparison across all model-dataset combinations, (B) Optimal threshold values and ranges across methods, (C) Accuracy preservation analysis, (D) Cross-model consistency evaluation.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Detailed Performance Analysis</span>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Scale-Invariant Universal</span>: Achieves highest computational savings (75.0% peak, 45.2% average) with remarkable cross-model consistency (CV = 4.5%). This method’s effect size normalization and coefficient of variation adjustment enable stable performance across different model families and entropy scales.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Information-Theoretic Optimal</span>: Delivers balanced performance (67.9% average savings) with strong theoretical foundations in mutual information maximization. The logarithmic scaling with effect size provides optimal information gain while maintaining conservative thresholds for uncertain distributions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bayesian Optimal</span>: Mathematically optimal decision boundary that minimizes classification error under Gaussian assumptions. Achieves similar performance to Information-Theoretic (65.3% average savings) with quadratic formulation enabling precise threshold placement.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Entropy Mean</span>: Conservative baseline ensuring perfect early-stop accuracy (100% confidence in gated subset) with modest computational savings (32.1% average). Requires minimal calibration data (5-10 examples) making it ideal for rapid deployment scenarios.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Key Takeaways and Strategic Implications</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Production Deployment Recommendations</span>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="A2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">High-Stakes Applications</span>: Use Entropy Mean for scenarios requiring guaranteed accuracy preservation with conservative early stopping. Ideal for medical, legal, or safety-critical reasoning tasks.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Balanced Production Systems</span>: Deploy Scale-Invariant Universal for optimal efficiency-accuracy trade-off with cross-model robustness. Recommended for general-purpose reasoning applications.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theoretically-Grounded Systems</span>: Implement Information-Theoretic or Bayesian Optimal when theoretical interpretability is crucial. Suitable for research applications requiring principled threshold justification.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Resource-Constrained Environments</span>: Scale-Invariant Universal provides maximum computational savings while maintaining accuracy, making it optimal for cost-sensitive deployments.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Threshold Methods: Complete Mathematical Derivations</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Information-Theoretic Optimal Threshold</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Information-Theoretic Optimal threshold is derived from mutual information maximization between entropy and correctness:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau_{\text{info}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>info</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau_{\text{info}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mu_{c}+\sigma_{c}\times\ln(1+|d|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mu_{c}+\sigma_{c}\times\ln(1+|d|)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is Cohen’s effect size. This threshold maximizes information gain while accounting for distribution overlap.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theoretical justification</span>: The logarithmic scaling with effect size ensures that:
1. Small effect sizes (<math id="A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|d|&lt;0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|d|&lt;0.5</annotation></semantics></math>) result in conservative thresholds near <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>
2. Large effect sizes (<math id="A3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|d|&gt;1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|d|&gt;1.0</annotation></semantics></math>) enable aggressive early stopping
3. The natural log provides smooth, theoretically grounded scaling</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Bayesian Optimal Threshold</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Derived from Bayesian decision theory, minimizing classification error under Gaussian assumptions:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau_{\text{bayes}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>bayes</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau_{\text{bayes}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{-b\pm\sqrt{b^{2}-4ac}}{2a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>±</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{-b\pm\sqrt{b^{2}-4ac}}{2a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sigma_{i}^{2}}-\frac{1}{\sigma_{c}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sigma_{i}^{2}}-\frac{1}{\sigma_{c}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\left(\frac{\mu_{c}}{\sigma_{c}^{2}}-\frac{\mu_{i}}{\sigma_{i}^{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\left(\frac{\mu_{c}}{\sigma_{c}^{2}}-\frac{\mu_{i}}{\sigma_{i}^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mu_{i}^{2}}{\sigma_{i}^{2}}-\frac{\mu_{c}^{2}}{\sigma_{c}^{2}}+2\ln\left(\frac{\sigma_{i}}{\sigma_{c}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mu_{i}^{2}}{\sigma_{i}^{2}}-\frac{\mu_{c}^{2}}{\sigma_{c}^{2}}+2\ln\left(\frac{\sigma_{i}}{\sigma_{c}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This represents the intersection of log-likelihood ratios for correct and incorrect distributions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Scale-Invariant Universal Threshold</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our novel Scale-Invariant Universal method derives a threshold that generalizes across model scales:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau_{\text{universal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>universal</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau_{\text{universal}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mu_{c}+\frac{\sqrt{|d|}}{1+\sqrt{|d|}}\times(\mu_{i}-\mu_{c})\times\max\left(0,1-\frac{\sigma_{c}}{\mu_{c}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mu_{c}+\frac{\sqrt{|d|}}{1+\sqrt{|d|}}\times(\mu_{i}-\mu_{c})\times\max\left(0,1-\frac{\sigma_{c}}{\mu_{c}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Components analysis</span>:</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sqrt{|d|}}{1+\sqrt{|d|}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sqrt{|d|}}{1+\sqrt{|d|}}</annotation></semantics></math>: Effect size normalization ensuring <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> range</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu_{i}-\mu_{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu_{i}-\mu_{c})</annotation></semantics></math>: Distribution separation magnitude</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\left(0,1-\frac{\sigma_{c}}{\mu_{c}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\left(0,1-\frac{\sigma_{c}}{\mu_{c}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>: Clamped coefficient of variation adjustment for scale invariance</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CV Handling</span>: The coefficient of variation (CV) term <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sigma_{c}}{\mu_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sigma_{c}}{\mu_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> can exceed 1 in high-noise scenarios, making <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\text{CV})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mtext>CV</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\text{CV})</annotation></semantics></math> negative. We apply clamping <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(0,1-\text{CV})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mtext>CV</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(0,1-\text{CV})</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure non-negative scaling factors. Alternative formulations include <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{1+\text{CV}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mtext>CV</mtext></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{1+\text{CV}}</annotation></semantics></math> for smooth monotonic decay, but empirically the clamped version provides better threshold stability.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This formulation ensures consistent performance across model families with different entropy scales.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Entropy Mean Threshold</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The simplest baseline method uses the mean of correct distribution:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau_{\text{mean}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>mean</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau_{\text{mean}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mu_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mu_{c}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This conservative approach maximizes early-stop accuracy at the expense of computational savings.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Statistical Methods Details</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Effect Size Calculation</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Cohen’s d effect size measures discriminative power between correct and incorrect entropy distributions:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=\frac{\mu_{i}-\mu_{c}}{\sigma_{\text{pooled}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>pooled</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=\frac{\mu_{i}-\mu_{c}}{\sigma_{\text{pooled}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\text{pooled}}=\sqrt{\frac{(n_{c}-1)\sigma_{c}^{2}+(n_{i}-1)\sigma_{i}^{2}}{n_{c}+n_{i}-2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>pooled</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\text{pooled}}=\sqrt{\frac{(n_{c}-1)\sigma_{c}^{2}+(n_{i}-1)\sigma_{i}^{2}}{n_{c}+n_{i}-2}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation guidelines</span>:</p>
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|d|&lt;0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|d|&lt;0.2</annotation></semantics></math>: Negligible effect</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.2\leq|d|&lt;0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.2\leq|d|&lt;0.5</annotation></semantics></math>: Small effect</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5\leq|d|&lt;0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5\leq|d|&lt;0.8</annotation></semantics></math>: Medium effect</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|d|\geq 0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|d|\geq 0.8</annotation></semantics></math>: Large effect (threshold for reliable discrimination)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Bootstrap Confidence Intervals</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All confidence intervals computed using bootstrap sampling (B=1000 iterations) with bias-corrected percentile method for robust statistical inference.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bootstrap procedure</span>:</p>
<ol id="A4.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sample <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> observations with replacement from original data</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Compute statistic of interest (accuracy, entropy, etc.)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Repeat <math id="A4.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=1000</annotation></semantics></math> times</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Calculate 2.5% and 97.5% percentiles for 95% CI</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Statistical Significance Testing</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Independent t-tests assess significance of entropy differences between correct and incorrect responses:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Null hypothesis</span>: <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}:\mu_{c}=\mu_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}:\mu_{c}=\mu_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (no discrimination)
<span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Alternative hypothesis</span>: <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}:\mu_{c}\neq\mu_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}:\mu_{c}\neq\mu_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (significant discrimination)</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Test statistic: <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\frac{\mu_{c}-\mu_{i}}{\sqrt{\frac{\sigma_{c}^{2}}{n_{c}}+\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{n_{i}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\frac{\mu_{c}-\mu_{i}}{\sqrt{\frac{\sigma_{c}^{2}}{n_{c}}+\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{n_{i}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Significance levels: * <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, ** <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, *** <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.001</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Experimental Configuration Details</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
